# Example fixtures are byte-exact test inputs; specs assert their sizes, so a
# Windows checkout must not convert their line endings.
examples/*/fixture/** -text
# Image-library specs count the encoded source bytes. Keep its text fixtures
# byte-identical on Windows instead of allowing core.autocrlf to add CR bytes.
examples/image-library/fixture/** text eol=lf
# The unreadable-image glyph is embedded as bytes and contributes to the same
# deterministic staged-byte counter as the fixture images.
examples/image-library/icons/unreadable.svg text eol=lf

# Dependency recipes and the notices they admit are identified by the hash of
# their exact bytes. A Windows checkout that rewrote their line endings would
# compute different digests and could neither reproduce nor publish a host.
dependencies/** -text

# The Windows resource is compiled from these and released beside the host, so
# its bytes must not depend on how a checkout wrote their line endings.
crates/host/windows/** -text

# The reviewed GPUI source tree and its original notices are byte-exact inputs.
# Preserve the published Metal shader's mixed indentation byte for byte.
